WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.260
A made up case.

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.780
Ravi is a land officer in a

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.900
busy town.

4
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.800
His stack of files has, by all

5
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.540
accounts, never once got

6
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.390
shorter.

7
00:00:11.865 --> 00:00:14.305
Today, one file stops him.

8
00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:16.825
The applicant is Sameer, his

9
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:18.205
college room mate.

10
00:00:18.205 --> 00:00:20.405
They once shared one blanket,

11
00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:23.035
and two exams' worth of panic.

12
00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:25.705
Sameer wants a no objection

13
00:00:25.705 --> 00:00:27.985
certificate for a shop on family

14
00:00:27.985 --> 00:00:31.265
land. The papers look fine.

15
00:00:31.265 --> 00:00:33.365
No one in the office knows they

16
00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.295
are friends.

17
00:00:34.891 --> 00:00:36.151
The dilemma:

18
00:00:36.151 --> 00:00:38.831
can Ravi judge a friend's file

19
00:00:38.831 --> 00:00:41.121
fairly, and be seen to?

20
00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:42.705
Option A:

21
00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:44.305
clear it quickly.

22
00:00:44.305 --> 00:00:45.925
Option B:

23
00:00:45.925 --> 00:00:47.845
reject it, to stay above

24
00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:50.345
suspicion. Option C:

25
00:00:50.345 --> 00:00:51.685
declare the friendship in

26
00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:53.565
writing, and ask for another

27
00:00:53.565 --> 00:00:57.195
officer. Pause here, and choose.

28
00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.480
Option A trusts a friendship,

29
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.920
not the file.

30
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.130
The rules ask for merit alone.

31
00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:08.216
Option B looks strict, but

32
00:01:08.216 --> 00:01:09.936
punishes Sameer for knowing

33
00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:13.446
Ravi. That is not fair either.

34
00:01:13.955 --> 00:01:16.115
Option C follows the Conduct

35
00:01:16.115 --> 00:01:18.895
Rules: declare a private

36
00:01:18.895 --> 00:01:20.755
interest, and resolve the

37
00:01:20.755 --> 00:01:23.025
conflict in the public interest.

38
00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:25.579
A sound answer names the

39
00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:28.459
conflict, writes it down, steps

40
00:01:28.459 --> 00:01:31.409
aside, and lets merit decide.

41
00:01:32.744 --> 00:01:33.484
For GS4:

42
00:01:33.484 --> 00:01:35.864
a friendship is not a crime.

43
00:01:35.864 --> 00:01:38.254
Hiding it is the problem.

44
00:01:39.192 --> 00:01:41.412
Ravi sends a short note to his

45
00:01:41.412 --> 00:01:44.652
senior. Then he calls Sameer,

46
00:01:44.652 --> 00:01:46.552
and they talk about everything,

47
00:01:46.552 --> 00:01:48.402
except the file.
